Description: DLNA/UPnP-AV media server for giant media folders
 microDLNA is a DLNA/UPnP-AV media server derived from MiniDLNA (aka
 ReadyMedia). By default it keeps no media database: each folder is read
 from disk when a client opens it, so it starts at once and copes with
 huge drives and folders holding many thousands of entries. Durations,
 thumbnails and folder counts are learned in memory as folders are used,
 and listings are sorted naturally by transliterated (pinyin) names.
 MiniDLNA's database mode is still available by setting db_dir.
 .
 The microdlnad daemon serves media files (music, pictures, and video) to
 clients on your network, such as VLC, Kodi, smart TVs and phones. It can
 run as a system service or be started by any user to share the current
 directory.
